summary:
  Whether a larger view is offered is decided without the screen's ratio.

history:
  On a screen scaled to 175% a cover of 300 was shown 600 wide in the
  page's units, 1050 of the screen's pixels: three and a half times its
  own, where the edges were seen to smear from three (measured on the
  panel, 2026-11-12). The limit is divided by the screen's ratio now. The
  offer asks the same rule, and has to hand it the same ratio: without it
  a view is promised at 600 and then drawn at 343, a tenth larger than the
  cover. This mutant decides the offer as on a screen that is not scaled.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CoverLogic.js

find:
      var page = coverScale(natW, natH, w, h), view = largerScale(natW, natH, roomW, roomH, ratio);

replace:
      var page = coverScale(natW, natH, w, h), view = largerScale(natW, natH, roomW, roomH, 1);

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_coverlogic.qml::test_a_view_only_a_little_larger_is_not_offered.
  Line-neutral.
